# C++ Data Types, Limits & Format Specifiers

## 1. Integer Data Types

| Data Type            | Typical Size | Minimum / Maximum Value                                 | Format Specifier |
| -------------------- | -----------: | ------------------------------------------------------- | ---------------- |
| `short`              |      2 bytes | -32,768 to 32,767                                       | `%hd`            |
| `unsigned short`     |      2 bytes | 0 to 65,535                                             | `%hu`            |
| `int`                |      4 bytes | -2,147,483,648 to 2,147,483,647                         | `%d`             |
| `unsigned int`       |      4 bytes | 0 to 4,294,967,295                                      | `%u`             |
| `long`               | 4 or 8 bytes | Platform dependent                                      | `%ld`            |
| `unsigned long`      | 4 or 8 bytes | Platform dependent                                      | `%lu`            |
| `long long`          |      8 bytes | -9,223,372,036,854,775,808 to 9,223,372,036,854,775,807 | `%lld`           |
| `unsigned long long` |      8 bytes | 0 to 18,446,744,073,709,551,615                         | `%llu`           |

### Example

```cpp
int age = 25;
long long population = 8000000000LL;

printf("%d\n", age);
printf("%lld\n", population);
```

