# 9. Format Specifiers for `printf`

## Integer

```text
%d       → int
%i       → int
%u       → unsigned int

%hd      → short
%hu      → unsigned short

%ld      → long
%lu      → unsigned long

%lld     → long long
%llu     → unsigned long long
```

## Floating Point

```text
%f       → floating-point output
%Lf      → long double
```

## Character

```text
%c       → char
```

## String

```text
%s       → C-style string
```

Example:

```cpp
char name[] = "John";

printf("%s", name);
```

---

# 10. Complete Example

```cpp
#include <iostream>
#include <cstdio>
using namespace std;

int main() {

    short a = 100;
    int b = 1000;
    long c = 100000;
    long long d = 10000000000LL;

    unsigned int e = 500;

    float f = 10.5f;
    double g = 99.999;
    long double h = 123.456L;

    char ch = 'A';
    bool status = true;

    printf("short: %hd\n", a);
    printf("int: %d\n", b);
    printf("long: %ld\n", c);
    printf("long long: %lld\n", d);

    printf("unsigned int: %u\n", e);

    printf("float: %f\n", f);
    printf("double: %f\n", g);
    printf("long double: %Lf\n", h);

    printf("char: %c\n", ch);
    printf("bool: %d\n", status);

    return 0;
}
```

