## Important C++ Note

When using C++ streams, you normally don't need format specifiers:

```cpp
cout << age;
cout << price;
cout << name;
```

Format specifiers such as `%d`, `%f`, `%lld`, etc. are mainly used with C-style functions such as:

```cpp
printf()
```
